spice-widget-egl: swap without waiting for the vblank

On X11 the display widget draws with its own EGL surface, and eglSwapBuffers
waited for the vblank. The widget redraws on every new scanout as well as on
every gl-draw (a guest flipping between buffers sends both each frame), so a
frame's gl-draw-done, which the server waits for, came up to a frame or more
late. The window is composited, so swapping right away doesn't tear.

--- a/src/spice-widget-egl.c
+++ b/src/spice-widget-egl.c
@@ -412,6 +412,13 @@
     if (!gl_make_current(display, err))
         return FALSE;
 
+    /*
+     * Don't wait for the vblank in eglSwapBuffers: the window is composited
+     * (no tearing), and a blocking swap delays the gl-draw-done that the
+     * server waits for, and each new scanout's redraws, by up to a frame each
+     */
+    eglSwapInterval(d->egl.display, 0);
+
     return TRUE;
 }
 
